  "steps": [
    {
      "step_id": "tile_python_while_loop_control.s01",
      "type": "explainer",
      "concept_ids": [
        "python.while_loops"
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Loops",
      "title": "Repeating while a condition holds: the while loop",
      "lede": "Keep processing deliveries as long as there are still orders to handle.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "block_id": "tile_python_while_loop_control.s01.h1",
          "text": "Repeating while a condition holds: the while loop",
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "block_id": "tile_python_while_loop_control.s01.p1",
          "text": "Sometimes you don't know in advance how many times you'll need to repeat something — you just want to keep going as long as some condition holds. A while loop executes its body repeatedly as long as its condition remains true; the condition can be a comparison, such as a < 10.",
          "role": "intro",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "python.while_loops"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "python.while_loops#f1"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "python.while_loops#tb1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "block_id": "tile_python_while_loop_control.s01.p2",
          "text": "The body is indented beneath the while line, and something in the body must change what the condition checks — otherwise the loop never stops:\n\npending = 3\nwhile pending > 0:\n    print('deliveries left:', pending)\n    pending = pending - 1\n\nEach pass prints the current count and decreases pending by 1, so the loop stops once pending reaches 0.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "python.while_loops"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "python.while_loops#f2"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "python.while_loops#tb2",
              "python.while_loops#tb3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "process_flow",
          "block_id": "tile_python_while_loop_control.s01.pf1",
          "title": "How a while loop re-checks its condition each pass",
          "direction": "TB",
