              "review_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gD8ePxAhjUM&t=178s",
              "start_seconds": 178,
              "end_seconds": 421,
              "label": "Visually explained: building a while-loop counter, including the infinite-loop trap and the fix",
              "summary": "Builds a counter with a while loop: write while, a condition such as i smaller than 4, and a body that prints i. Without first assigning i the code fails, so the clip sets i to 1 before the loop. It then traces why the loop never ends when nothing changes i, and fixes that by adding 1 to i on each pass, tracing i from 1 to 4 until the condition becomes false and the loop exits. The recap names three parts: an initial value before the loop, the condition, and an update inside the body.",
              "fact_ids": [
