      "title": "Steering mid-loop: break and continue",
      "lede": "Exit a loop early or skip a bad record without stopping the whole loop.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "block_id": "tile_python_while_loop_control.s05.h1",
          "text": "Steering mid-loop: break and continue",
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "block_id": "tile_python_while_loop_control.s05.p1",
          "text": "The break statement exits the innermost enclosing for or while loop immediately — useful for stopping a search over delivery orders as soon as the one you want is found. The continue statement skips the rest of the current iteration and moves to the next one — for example, skipping a delivery record that's missing a time without exiting the whole loop.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "python.loop_control"
