      "title": "The body must change what the condition checks",
      "lede": "Let's revisit why the loop body must update the condition variable.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "block_id": "tile_python_while_loop_control.r01.h1",
          "text": "Reminder: the body must change what the condition checks",
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "block_id": "tile_python_while_loop_control.r01.p1",
          "text": "The body of a while loop must change what the condition checks — otherwise the condition stays true forever and the loop never stops. In the pending example, pending = pending - 1 decreases pending each pass, so pending > 0 eventually becomes false and the loop exits.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
