      "title": "continue vs break",
      "lede": "Let's revisit the difference between continue and break.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "block_id": "tile_python_while_loop_control.r02.h1",
          "text": "Reminder: continue vs break",
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "block_id": "tile_python_while_loop_control.r02.p1",
          "text": "continue skips the rest of the current iteration and moves to the next one — the loop keeps running. break exits the innermost loop entirely — no more iterations happen. Use continue to skip a bad record; use break to stop searching once you've found what you need.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "python.loop_control"
            ],
